# dbt modeling layers

Pipeline: landing files → DuckDB `raw` (ingest) → `stg_` → `int_` → `fct_` / `dim_`.

| Layer | Location / naming | Role |
|-------|-------------------|------|
| Landing | `data/landing/itbi/` (+ other source subdirs) | Yearly ITBI `.xlsx` (sheets = months); not queried by models |
| Raw | schema `raw`, `source('raw', ...)` | As-ingested; full replace per file; no incremental |
| Staging | `stg_*` | Rename, cast, dedupe; **views only — never incremental** |
| Intermediate | `int_*` | Joins and shared logic; views by default |
| Marts | `dim_*` tables; `fct_*` **incremental + merge** | Analysis-ready; see `docs/modeling.md` |

Materializations: staging/intermediate = view; marts folder default = table; **override `fct_*` to `incremental` + `unique_key` + `incremental_strategy='merge'`**.

- One model per file; document grain and primary keys in `schema.yml`.
- Staging reads only from `source('raw', ...)`.
- After re-ingest (new month or historical correction): `dbt run`; use `--full-refresh` on a fact after logic changes.
- When adding a new XLSX source table, update `models/staging/_sources.yml`.
- Run `dbt test` after model changes (see `data-tdd.mdc`).
